## Correction record — a mistyped commit id reported to the reviewers

An earlier status report quoted the build-exit correction commit as
`e46a165b4f0d6d5b6a1e8c0d6f0c9f5b0a4b3c2d`. **That value never existed**; it was
typed by hand instead of read from git, and the tail after the short prefix was
fabricated.

- Detected by: the reviewer, via the GitHub API, which returned the real object.
- Actual value: `e46a165a723fa279071e13dd68c23efbf64c3bf1`
  (`git log -1 --format=%H e46a165`).
- Corrected: 2026-10-22, in this file and in the PR body, before any merge.
- Rule adopted: commit ids are copied from `git rev-parse` / `git log --format=%H`
  output, never from working memory; every id quoted in the PR body carries the
  command that produces it.
